<h2>5. Generate SQL</h2>

<p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>G</kbd> (<kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>G</kbd> on macOS), or <strong>Database → Generate DDL…</strong>:</p>

<pre><code>CREATE TABLE "users" (
	"user_id" integer NOT NULL GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY,
	"email" varchar(255) NOT NULL,
	"created_at" timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
	CONSTRAINT "pk_users" PRIMARY KEY("user_id")
);

CREATE TABLE "orders" (
	"order_id" integer NOT NULL GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY,
	"user_id" integer,
	CONSTRAINT "pk_orders" PRIMARY KEY("order_id")
);

CREATE INDEX "ix_orders_user_id" ON "orders" (
	"user_id"
);

ALTER TABLE "orders" ADD CONSTRAINT "fk_orders_user_id" FOREIGN KEY ("user_id")
	REFERENCES "users"("user_id")
	ON DELETE RESTRICT
	ON UPDATE RESTRICT
	NOT DEFERRABLE;</code></pre>

<p>Foreign keys always come after all tables are created. Copy the SQL, save it with <strong>Save .sql…</strong>, or pipe it to <code>psql</code> from the CLI with <code>pgdesigner generate</code>.</p>

<h2>6. Lint your schema</h2>

<p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> (<kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd>) or <strong>Diagram → Check Diagram</strong>. PgDesigner runs 69 rules and reports errors, warnings, and suggestions — fixable issues get a fix button.</p>

<h2>7. Save and commit</h2>

<p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd> (<strong>File → Save As…</strong>) and save the project into your repository as a <code>.pgd</code> file. Then commit it:</p>

<pre><code>git add shop.pgd
git commit -m "Initial schema: users + orders"</code></pre>

<p>From now on, every schema change produces a clean single-line diff in your pull requests.</p>

